  {
   "id": "brief-1",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -150,
   "w": 560,
   "page": "page-1",
   "text": "Brownie v2 \u2014 the bets on top of the shipping app.\n\nClick around the prototype: Loops in the sidebar, the Rohan card \u2192 brief, the Sunday letter, Recipes \u2192 Teach Hands (a 3-step flow), the footer link \u2192 What left your Mac, Settings \u2192 Brain \u2192 This Mac only, Settings \u2192 Privacy \u2192 Erase everything.\n\nFirst-time tips play once per new screen and complete on the action, as in v1."
  },
  {
   "id": "kb-note",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -170,
   "w": 620,
   "page": "page-3",
   "text": "Knowledge as the product \u2014 four screens to react to.\n\n1 \u00b7 Ask: every claim carries a chip; clicking opens the original chat, mail or note.\n2 \u00b7 Notes: the knowledge base is an Obsidian vault \u2014 [[wikilinks]], Open in Obsidian, a mirror in iCloud Drive for the phone.\n3 \u00b7 Settings \u2192 Knowledge: vault location, Obsidian, iCloud; and \u201cLet your other AIs read your notes\u201d \u2014 Brownie as an MCP server that runs ON THIS MAC only (no hosting, no port, no account): Claude Desktop / Cursor / Raycast start it on demand. ChatGPT needs a public URL, so it's marked not possible. Per-app allow list and a log of what each app asked.\n4 \u00b7 Settings \u2192 Overnight: reads during the day every hour / 3 hours, only when idle and on power."
  }
